aintegral audio filter (src/audio/aintegral.ts)

src/audio/aintegral.ts adapts the aintegral filter of FFmpeg
libavfilter/af_aderivative.c (ff_af_aintegral, the INTEGRAL(flt, float) and
INTEGRAL(dbl, double) loops, config_input and filter_frame): a per-channel
running sum that starts at zero and carries across frames, computed in float
for fltp and in double for dblp, over the native FILTER_SAMPLEFMTS list
(fltp, dblp).

Fixed FFmpeg commit:946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8
libavfilter/af_aderivative.c carries no individual copyright line; its header
states only "This file is part of FFmpeg."
LGPL-2.1-or-later. See LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.
The TypeScript adaptation is a separate module: it shares no code with
aderivative, accepts no options, and refuses timeline enable and commands
instead of implementing ctx->is_disabled. It adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
